  "_comment": "What this repo's sources were last checked against. The monthly 'Standards watch' workflow fails (and GitHub emails the failure) when upstream has moved past a value below; the failure names the rules that cite that source (through the entry's rule_sources URL prefixes). To update: review the change, set the new value and its reviewed/verified date, and set changed_on to the same date. Then re-read every rule the failure named and set its last_verified date: until then Static Checks (stale_rules.py) fails for each rule that cites the source and is older than changed_on. Trade-off sections named in the failure have no date, so re-reading them is not checked. For OWASP the failure includes a compare link and the cheat sheet's own diff.",
